      "extract": "Introduction There are several variations of the deﬁnition of the Bloch group in the litera- ture; by [7] they diﬀer at most by torsion and they agree with each other for algebraically closed ﬁelds. In this paper we shall use the following. Deﬁnition 1.1 Let k be a ﬁeld. The pre-Bloch group P(k) is the quotient of the free Z–module Z(k −{0, 1}) by all instances of the following relation: [x] −[y] + [y x] −[1 −x−1 1",
